      {
        "id": "U7-D5",
        "statement": "confirm-notice checks the answer first (exact, case-sensitive \u0027delivered\u0027 or \u0027not-delivered\u0027; anything else gives InvalidInput \u0027answer must be delivered or not-delivered\u0027). It then looks for an active loan of the copy with an unknown notice. An unknown copy gets the same \u0027no unknown notice for \u003Ccopy\u003E\u0027 error (new LendingError NoUnknownNotice), as R2 specifies for any copy without an unknown notice. Confirmed delivered is kept as NoticeConfirmedDelivered, so the record shows staff confirmed it.",
